  "final_message": "<think>Now let me write the test setup. I'll add a vitest config in vite.config.ts (test section) \u2014 but that requires the `/// <reference types=\"vitest/config\" />` or defineConfig from vitest/config. Let me create a separate `vitest.config.ts` to keep vite.config.ts clean... but then the tailwind plugin isn't needed for tests (no CSS processing needed; vitest handles CSS imports by stubbing them).\n\nActually, simpler: create `vitest.config.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    globals: true,\n    setupFiles: \"./src/test/setup.ts\",\n    include: [\"src/**/*.test.tsx\", \"src/**/*.test.ts\"],\n  },\n});\n```\n\nAnd add a \"test\": \"vitest run\" script to package.json.\n\nNow the test file: src/__tests__/app.test.tsx\n\nMock fetch with a simple in-memory implementation of the API routes.\n\nLet me write a fake fetch:\n\n```ts\nfunction jsonResponse(body: unknown, status = 200) {\n  return new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" } });\n}\n```\njsdom in Node 22+ has Response available (undici) \u2713 (Node 24 here). vitest's jsdom environment provides fetch? The global fetch comes from Node \u2713.\n\nMock:\n```ts\nconst state = { users: new Map<string, {password: string; id: number}>(), tokens: new Map<string, number>(), conversions: [] };\n```\n\nThen `vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", mockFetch)`.\n\nLet me write the mock fetch to handle:\n- POST /api/auth/register\n- POST /api/auth/login\n- GET /api/auth/me\n- POST /api/base64/encode\n- POST /api/base64/decode\n- GET /api/conversions\n- POST /api/conversions\n- DELETE /api/conversions/:id\n\nThen the tests:\n1. renders the converter and encodes text.\n2. shows the API error message for invalid base64.\n3. registers and signs in \u2192 shows the username and sign-out button.\n4. signed-in user: save to history switch \u2192 history list \u2192 delete \u2192 paging.\n\nAnd crucially, assert the accessibility queries that a Playwright test would use:\n- getByLabel(\"Username\") is unique (getAllByLabel length === 1)\n- getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Encode\" }) etc.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nNote: @testing-library/user-event with fake timers isn't needed.\n\nLet me write the testfile.</think>\n\n",
